<title>ITALY: MOTORCYCLING-WORLD SUPERBIKE CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-WORLD SUPERBIKE CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MONZA, Italy 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in the</p>
<p>fifth round of superbike world championship on Sunday (both</p>
<p>races 18 laps, 103.800 kms)</p>
<p>First race</p>
<p> 1. John Kocinski (U.S.) Honda    32 minutes 41.944 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Aaron Slight (New Zealand) Honda	32:41.949</p>
<p> 3. Carl Fogarty (Britain) Ducati	   32:41.952</p>
<p> 4. Simon Crafar (New Zealand) Kawasaki   32:42.326</p>
<p> 5. Scott Russell (U.S.) Yamaha	     32:42.573</p>
<p> 6. Jamie Whitham (Britain) Suzuki	  32:48.717</p>
<p> 7. Pier-Francesco Chili (Italy) Ducati   32:49.028</p>
<p> 8. Akira Yanagawa (Japan) Kawasaki	 32:49.079</p>
<p> 9. Piergiorgio Bontempi (Italy) Kawasaki 32:54.324</p>
<p> 10.Mike Hale (U.S.) Suzuki		   32:56.632</p>
<p>Second race</p>
<p> 1. Chili					   36:46.817</p>
<p> 2. Kocinski					36:48.657</p>
<p> 3. Whitham					 36:53.905</p>
<p> 4. Fogarty					 36:55.165</p>
<p> 5. Slight					  37:27.241</p>
<p> 6. Bontempi					37:32.864</p>
<p> 7. Crafar					  37:34.437</p>
<p> 8. Russell					 37:36.500</p>
<p> 9. Hale					    38:08.093</p>
<p> 10. Jochen Schmid (Germany) Kawasaki     38:09.446</p>
<p>World championship standings after five rounds:</p>
<p> 1. Fogarty					 177 points</p>
<p> 2. Kocinski					163</p>
<p> 3. Slight					  155</p>
<p> 4. Crafar					  113</p>
<p> 5. Chili					    99</p>
<p> 6. Russell					  96</p>
<p> 7. Colin Edwards (U.S.) Yamaha		79</p>
<p> 8. Whitham					  63</p>
<p> 9 equal. Yanagawa				 60</p>
<p> 9 equal. Neil Hodgson (Britain) Ducati    60</p>
